#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:9
#: 85b449250c624a268e470d3801f34b7d
msgid "Soaring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:14
#: bf93397448d3431c99ae3161cfcf09d4
msgid "The autonomous soaring functionality in ArduPilot allows the plane to respond to rising air current (thermals) in order to extend endurance and gain altitude with minimal use of the motor (soaring). Its full technical description is available in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:18
#: 36aa684e67484fd7b4c968659f0ea65f
msgid "*S. Tabor, I. Guilliard, A. Kolobov.* `ArduSoar: an Open-Source Thermalling Controller for Resource-Constrained Autopilots <https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08215/>`_. *International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS), 2018.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:20
#: 7a9bbc8cb7314e7383bab5bfeec944dc
msgid "Use of an airspeed sensor is strongly recommended in order to obtain optimum performance. Use without a sensor could yield unsatisfactory results. Consistent operation without an airspeed sensor is a pending future development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:24
#: 58ea25c3308a44d1a4ca6f2b30197782
msgid "This picture shows the different phases of flight when using the soaring functionality:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:27
#: 3f427333f5274af785e86441a057e961
msgid "If modes AUTO, FBWB or CRUISE are entered, and Soaring is enabled, the throttle is set to zero provided the aircraft is above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` altitude and the aircraft then begins gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:28
#: a813d33c7e984972a69aa3638724d152
msgid "If the aircraft descends to :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` altitude, throttle is re-enabled and the aircraft will begin to climb to the altitude of the next waypoint, in AUTO, or to :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude in CRUISE or FBWB. In AUTO, if the waypoint altitude is less than :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, then Soaring can not begin before reaching the waypoint. If it is above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, then Soaring can occur once that altitude has been reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:29
#: 4ed761cdf9774428904660628fd73f0e
msgid "When the aircraft reaches :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, throttle is set to zero again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:30
#: 16e790ff6a5b4dd0ad58ca343cf3395e
msgid "If, during gliding flight, the air is estimated to be rising at more than :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` and the :ref:`RC switch position<soaring_rc-switch>` allows it, the aircraft will automatically enter THERMAL mode. While in THERMAL mode the aircraft will adjust the circling position to better centre the thermal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:32
#: 3511a7ed2a8a4057a186b9d796af5bb6
msgid "THERMAL mode is exited under the following conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:34
#: 217425c0e532470cb647df58331e9ee0
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MAX<SOAR_ALT_MAX>` is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:35
#: 5a1c599d237746c7bbb534149baf3f67
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:36
#: d2d66844d2254ba8a7c8e54197300cb6
msgid "Flight mode is changed by the pilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:37
#: 7160263d494c41c281442b68ffb7f1af
msgid "The estimate of achievable climb rate falls below :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>`, and thermalling has lasted at least :ref:`SOAR_MIN_THML_S<SOAR_MIN_THML_S>` seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:39
#: dc951fa5acf1455db736f7d6f7a5bd18
msgid "The aircraft drifts more than :ref:`SOAR_MAX_DRIFT<SOAR_MAX_DRIFT>` - see :ref:`Limit maximum distance from home<soaring_maximum-distance-from-home>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:41
#: 4116172fb1364cfcbcbca472c87b91c6
msgid "The flight mode will be returned to whatever it was before THERMAL was triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:44
#: ffe7a3122223429093376ed1f3fbd5a5
msgid "Airspeed Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:46
#: db06cdc2ff0947219f337869b4c56e0e
msgid "When in SOARING, the target airspeed while cruising is set via throttle stick position for FBWB and CRUISE modes, even while gliding. For AUTO mode, it is set at  :ref:`AIRSPEED_CRUISE<AIRSPEED_CRUISE>`, unless the :ref:`SOAR_CRSE_ARSPD<SOAR_CRSE_ARSPD>` parameter is set to a non-zero value (\"0\" is default). If it is set to \"-1\", then the :ref:`soaring-speed-to-fly` computed value will be used. If greater than zero, then that value in meters/sec will be used for target airspeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:48
#: 051ddd8754d84f3fb64ef657254e8fd4
msgid "While in THERMAL mode, the target airspeed will be :ref:`AIRSPEED_CRUISE<AIRSPEED_CRUISE>`, unless the :ref:`SOAR_THML_ARSPD<SOAR_THML_ARSPD>` parameter is set to a non-zero value (\"0\" is default). Then that value in meters/sec will be used for target airspeed instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:52
#: f075d0a002bc469c8a6c7cf51eed1a47
msgid "Hardware"
msgstr ""

