#: 5c716c2f1bff407288369586b82a0755
msgid "Set the parameter :ref:`SOAR_ENABLE<SOAR_ENABLE>` to 1 and refresh the parameters. This will allow the other SOAR parameters to appear in the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:85
#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:186
#: 509da83803794e72ad1ee4ceff1db8d5
#: f5f649df0bb04a4bbcd676094c7b9dba
msgid "Drag Polar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:87
#: 357aab66d8bc4b8aba1bda6c00dbd8e9
msgid "To work out how fast the air is rising or sinking the autopilot needs to know the aircraft's sink rate for a given airspeed in still air. This is related to the drag polar of the plane and is specified using the SOAR_POLAR parameters. :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` is the most important one to set initially and is calculated using the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:93
#: d9e09335b7a94cb69f8dd6ded638f7f7
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` = 16*Weight/Area (weight in kg, area in metres squared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:96
#: c5d343153bb34389ac8af15b58a3d9e6
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` = 703*Weight/Area (weight in oz, area in inches squared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:99
#: cfd7b89a470d40f5ab231ddb9dd77316
msgid "Calculating the other parameters is explained under tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:104
#: c7be03545aa84e1b98051ac9b4af8d68
msgid "RC switch (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:106
#: 8b6c2b6e8b4f4c4a85fd192222dbf145
msgid "You can use a 3-position RC switch to control when the autopilot can use soaring. Set the parameter RCX_OPTION parameter for the desired channel to SOAR (index 88) - see :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>`. The 3 positions have the following effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:108
#: bd6c8a053da646879b4936be74b26e6b
msgid "Low. Soaring is disabled (equivalent to setting SOAR_ENABLE = 0). Throttle will be used as normal. Switching to this from either of the positions below, will disable Soaring and maintain the current flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:110
#: cb262c8dc88b4ca9b064edb318c114c2
msgid "Mid. Soaring will have control over throttle. The mode will not automatically change to THERMAL based on detected rising air. However, when manually set to THERMAL mode using RC controller or GCS, the autopilot will try to follow rising air currents. It will still restore the previous mode if the aircraft is not climbing, or if it drifts too far (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:112
#: 7c5f3e1de06f482e9d680dc660695f00
msgid "High. Fully automatic mode changes to THERMAL from AUTO, FBWB or CRUISE modes in response to detected rising air, and following of rising air currents."
msgstr ""

