#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:131
#: 017cefea0b70421eabd5d1dd713be631
msgid "Set limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:133
#: ba39f66232694466bff45ddf215878b2
msgid "Because the soaring feature can follow rising air as required to gain altitude, it is important to set limits to avoid it leaving the original flight area completely. This is especially important in windy conditions as the autopilot will try to follow thermals downwind. There are three ways to set limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:136
#: d08001ac218b4cbf84fba05999dd259b
msgid "Altitude limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:138
#: fdd655c1420e440da65517c1d199eeb6
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MAX<SOAR_ALT_MAX>` sets the altitude you want the autopilot to stop thermalling. :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` sets the minimum altitude you want the autopilot to descend to while gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:143
#: bad84766feec479d9306a19b93055ef8
msgid "Spatial limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:145
#: 27a00f13d4414f08bb625222e86665b3
msgid "The parameter :ref:`SOAR_MAX_DRIFT<SOAR_MAX_DRIFT>` can be used to limit how far (in metres) the aircraft can drift while in THERMAL mode. If the aircraft reaches this limit in THERMAL mode, it will revert to the original flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:147
#: 8f46e19e5eba4cd6865f459f325bcfd9
msgid "If the original flight mode was FBWB or CRUISE mode, the drift distance is measured from the location THERMAL was entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:149
#: 9e89b8d681ff4bf78504b7be817297cd
msgid "If the original flight mode was AUTO mode, the drift distance is measured from the closest point on the mission segment to where THERMAL was entered. Drift sideways or backwards, but not along the original mission track, is counted. This allows thermalling to continue if the wind is moving the aircraft in the direction of the next waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:153
#: ec17460064a74f3fbf076834f9d6a038
msgid "The image below shows a scenario where the mission track is north to south and the wind is causing thermals to drift east to west. The aircraft will follow them but will respect :ref:`SOAR_MAX_DRIFT<SOAR_MAX_DRIFT>`. Note that sometimes it will go a little beyond  :ref:`SOAR_MAX_DRIFT<SOAR_MAX_DRIFT>` as it lines up its heading to the next waypoint before reverting to AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:158
#: 3a96c724cede44358c4d6c6bc9e1f216
msgid "If using FBWB or CRUISE mode, the parameter :ref:`SOAR_MAX_RADIUS<SOAR_MAX_RADIUS>` can be used to trigger RTL if the aircraft is more than this distance from home when in THERMAL mode. Note that this parameter won't stop the aircraft from exceeding this distance before it enters THERMAL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:160
#: 56c3baa09c824924a8d979a67a36eae3
msgid ":ref:`Geofence <geofencing>` can be used as a last line of defence. Set it up in the usual way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:165
#: 4bd1977751cf4855b7378aecb6d01e90
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:168
#: 458e4a4c014b489a9d5c040b29b29c9e
msgid "Triggering lift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:170
#: 369879cc7af64ad8b7e2d5ffc2a67312
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` controls when the mode will be changed to THERMAL. The default of 0.7m/s may be too low if you fly in strong conditions. Increasing this value makes the aircraft more \"picky\" about the lift it will try to circle in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:175
#: 9ffa38cb73a24c8680c1bfbc089807b9
msgid "Thermalling bank angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:177
#: 417f4f3b68b346d4a21313e0066e0c00
msgid "The parameter :ref:`SOAR_THML_BANK<SOAR_THML_BANK>` sets the bank angle when thermalling. 30 - 45 degrees works well depending on the size of the thermals in your area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:179
#: 69d163a6e5c74a0da29fead1ee65e335
msgid "If the aircraft is not achieving this average bank angle when thermalling, you should check -"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:181
#: 71d6ddc935a24fdd954f4963c4d642d9
msgid "that the limiting bank angle :ref:`ROLL_LIMIT_DEG<ROLL_LIMIT_DEG>` is set a bit larger than SOAR_THML_BANK (note the units are different) to give some room for manoeuvring;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:183
#: 382b10057fc24bd98bcc0886d9b7c5b9
msgid "that the navigation parameter NAVL1_PERIOD is no larger than the time needed for a complete turn at the specified bank angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:188
#: 3b574f80a5134e2aad5fad6265df8809
msgid "While the default settings for :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_B<SOAR_POLAR_B>` and :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_CD0<SOAR_POLAR_CD0>` should be OK for most foamie-style glider aircraft, improving the accuracy of these parameters will improve how your aircraft detects and centres lift. You can use `this spreadsheet <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WA9CXRSPBc6mFydhQ3O_2SeDrQoFH1UrdiXd0PJ-zE4/edit?usp=sharing>`__ to calculate better values from glide tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:193
#: 434864c1db1b4f60abfeb4854e684d29
msgid "Time hysteresis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:195
#: fd80e3f2312244c39ec257330387c45b
msgid "Adding hysteresis can reduce the frequency of mode changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:197
#: 06456b85cbc946c69c4e3136f7456ac6
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_MIN_THML_S<SOAR_MIN_THML_S>`: Minimum time to remain in THERMAL once entered for a thermal before exiting due to low lift or altitude limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:199
#: 39a8fc58ec0f44c4ba34a6f155e8f576
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_MIN_CRSE_S<SOAR_MIN_CRSE_S>`: Minimum time to remain in glide after exiting THERMAL due to low lift or altitude limits before entering mode again, or when entering Soaring initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:202
#: 3b8a1e102e284bbdb269866419c37c07
msgid "TECS Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:206
#: 395bf2cf25c64487bb66d59d67c12181
msgid "In firmware revisions before 4.1, it was necessary to set :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` to 2.0 when using soaring. This is now handled automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:209
#: 52531993ee7a467786ad1e5fd843c8e3
msgid "For best results the TECS needs to be set up to fly the aircraft at a consistent airspeed when gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:212
#: fb989459d2dc45a996f37e9ea7bc63d3
msgid "If your aircraft has trouble maintaining airspeed accurately you can tune it by confirming that :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` is set to 2.0, :ref:`SOAR_ENABLE<SOAR_ENABLE>` to 1 and set :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` to a large number, say 50.0, or use the :ref:`RC switch<soaring_rc-switch-upcoming>` to inhibit mode changes. This means that the aircraft will glide but will never begin thermalling. Set :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` to an altitude high enough to allow a good length of time to be spent gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:219
#: 0286ea194039410f8c6be171a7247af3
msgid "Launch the aircraft and put it in AUTO mode. It should climb to :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` and then begin a gliding descent. Watch the telemetry graphs or look at the Dataflash logs after the flight. Is the aircraft maintaining the demanded airspeed? The actual and demanded airspeed can be seen in the onboard log as ``TECS.sp`` and ``TECS.spdem``, and via telemetry you can use ``NAV_CONTROLLER_OUTPUT.aspd_error``. Problems can usually be fixed by increasing ``PTCH2SRV_IMAX`` and :ref:`TECS_INTEG_GAIN<TECS_INTEG_GAIN>` to achieve good airspeed tracking in gliding flight."
msgstr ""

