#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:239
#: 3ecd81bef927447397ec4c9b8e055d2a
msgid "Currently, the only effect on telemetry is that when soaring is active the climb rate item (VFR_HUD.climb) is altered. Rather that the estimated vertical speed of the aircraft, the estimated vertical speed of the air mass is sent. This field is used by Mission Planner and OpenTX radios to produce vario audio output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:242
#: c70475e2429c47c19dfbe05f48089b60
msgid "Use of TECS synthetic airspeed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-4_1.rst:244
#: 0f0036f5788f4782b1d9b5b32080dbde
msgid "If your plane can't accommodate an airspeed sensor, it is possible to use the TECS synthetic airspeed estimate :ref:`TECS_SYNAIRSPEED<TECS_SYNAIRSPEED>`. Make sure you read the warning regarding this feature before deciding to use it. To use this feature, set the parameter :ref:`TECS_SYNAIRSPEED<TECS_SYNAIRSPEED>` to 1."
msgstr ""
